  "question": "The database is utilized for managing data on the network cultural relics protection platform. Its primary functions include recording basic relic information, repair history, exhibition information, and environmental monitoring data. Through the management and association of these data, the full lifecycle protection of cultural relics in a digital environment is ensured.\n\n1. Cultural Relic  \n   Function: Store basic information of the cultural relic.  \n   Fields: Cultural Relic ID, Name, Year, Category, Excavation Site  \n   Business Requirement: This data is used to store the basic information of all cultural relics on the platform, such as name and repair history, for the purpose of querying and management.\n\n2. Staff  \n   Function: Record information of staff on the cultural relics protection platform.  \n   Fields: Staff ID, Name, Phone Number, Gender  \n   Business Requirement: This data is used to record information of staff related to cultural relic protection, aiding administrators in tracking staff identity and contact information.\n\n3. Cultural Relic Exhibition  \n   Function: Record exhibition information of the cultural relic.  \n   Fields: Cultural Relic ID, Exhibition Start Time, Exhibition End Time, Exhibition Location  \n   Business Requirement: Record cultural relic exhibition events, including the time and location of the exhibition, facilitating management and querying of the cultural relic's exhibition history.\n\n4. Cultural Relic Repair  \n   Function: Record repair history of the cultural relic.  \n   Fields: Staff ID, Cultural Relic ID, Repair Start Time, Repair End Time, Repair Method, Notes  \n   Business Requirement: Used to record each repair activity of the cultural relic, including repair start and end times, repair method, and repairing staff, aiding cultural relic administrators in tracking the repair history.\n\n5. Cultural Relic Monitoring Record  \n   Function: Record environmental monitoring data of the cultural relic.  \n   Fields: Cultural Relic ID, Monitoring Time, Person in Charge ID, Temperature, Humidity, Light, Air Quality, Notes  \n   Business Requirement: Used to record the environmental data (such as temperature, humidity, light, etc.) of the cultural relic in specific time periods, ensuring the preservation environment of the cultural relic meets standards and documenting monitoring history.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0504\nCREATE TABLE `cultural_relic` (\n  `cultural_relic_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `year` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `category` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `excavation_site` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`cultural_relic_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `staff` (\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`staff_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cultural_relic_exhibition` (\n  `exhibition_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cultural_relic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `exhibition_start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `exhibition_end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `exhibition_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`exhibition_id`),\n  KEY `cultural_relic_exhibition_ibfk_1` (`cultural_relic_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cultural_relic_exhibition_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cultural_relic_id`) REFERENCES `cultural_relic` (`cultural_relic_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cultural_relic_repair` (\n  `repair_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `staff_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `cultural_relic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `repair_start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `repair_end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `repair_method` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`repair_id`),\n  KEY `cultural_relic_repair_ibfk_1` (`staff_id`),\n  KEY `cultural_relic_repair_ibfk_2` (`cultural_relic_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cultural_relic_repair_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`staff_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `cultural_relic_repair_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`cultural_relic_id`) REFERENCES `cultural_relic` (`cultural_relic_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cultural_relic_monitoring_record` (\n  `monitoring_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cultural_relic_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `monitoring_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `temperature` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `humidity` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `light` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `air_quality` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `notes` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`monitoring_record_id`),\n  KEY `cultural_relic_monitoring_record_ibfk_1` (`cultural_relic_id`),\n  KEY `cultural_relic_monitoring_record_ibfk_2` (`person_in_charge_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cultural_relic_monitoring_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cultural_relic_id`) REFERENCES `cultural_relic` (`cultural_relic_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `cultural_relic_monitoring_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge_id`) REFERENCES `staff` (`staff_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
